## Key Architectural Patterns Summary

| Concern | Approach |
|---|---|
| Ktor version | 3.4.0 |
| Engine: Android | `ktor-client-cio` |
| Engine: JVM | `ktor-client-cio` |
| Engine: iOS | `ktor-client-darwin` |
| Engine: Web (Wasm/JS) | `ktor-client-js-wasm-js` |
| Engine in commonMain | None — only `ktor-client-core` |
| Debug/release logging | Gradle-time selection via `local.properties` flag, not runtime |
| Interface vs impl | `coreNetworkApi` has zero transitive deps; `coreNetworkKtor`/`coreNetworkStub` are mutually exclusive at link time |
| Koin | Both Ktor and Stub modules export the same `val coreNetworkModule` — swap by changing which module the app depends on |
| Error handling | `runCatching` + `fold` into `NetworkResult.Success`/`NetworkResult.Failure` |
| DTO/domain split | Internal `HitResponse` (serialization-annotated) lives only in `coreNetworkKtor`; public `HitModel` lives in `coreNetworkApi` |
| Stub data | Real asset files bundled via Compose Multiplatform resources, accessed with `Res.getUri()` |

